  "identifier": "neuro-jepa",
  "name": "Neuro-JEPA",
  "alternateName": [
    "Sparse Latent Predictive Foundation Model for Multimodal Neuroimaging"
  ],
  "description": "Foundation model for multimodal volumetric brain MRI that extends the V-JEPA 2 joint-embedding predictive architecture to 3D and combines a latent predictive objective with a sparse Mixture-of-Experts backbone (3D ViT-Base-MoE, 96×108×96 voxels). Adds foreground-aware objectives and improved masking for T1-weighted, T2-weighted, and FLAIR sequences. Pretrained on ~1.55 million curated scans from 428,647 studies across 282,693 patients at NYU Langone, and evaluated across 47 downstream tasks spanning diagnosis, prognosis, regression, multimodal learning, and time-to-event prediction over 12 public cohorts plus 3 large clinical cohorts (NYU Langone, NYU Long Island, Massachusetts General Hospital). Reports average gains of 4.4–6.4% AUROC on unimodal and 5.8–7.6% AUROC on multimodal tasks over prior neuroimaging foundation models and CNN baselines. Code is MIT; model weights are gated and released under CC-BY-NC-ND-4.0 (non-commercial, no derivatives).",
  "url": "https://huggingface.co/NYUMedML/Neuro-JEPA",
  "codeRepository": "https://github.com/NYUMedML/Neuro-JEPA",
  "relatedLink": [
    "https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.14957",
    "https://github.com/NYUMedML/Neuro-JEPA"
  ],
